{"id": "EUVD-2026-80402", "enisaUuid": "34858210-cd60-3ac4-b1e9-5c684d66a4a9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau/uvmm: fix NULL deref unwinding an OP_MAP_SPARSE op\n\nEach bind_job_op is zeroed by kzalloc_obj() in bind_job_op_from_uop(),\nand the OP_MAP_SPARSE case in nouveau_uvmm_bind_job_submit() only creates\na region, so op->ops stays NULL for a successfully processed sparse map.\n\nIf a later op in the same job fails, the reverse unwind loop revisits that\nop and calls drm_gpuva_ops_free(&uvmm->base, op->ops) unconditionally.\ndrm_gpuva_ops_free() dereferences its argument right away\n(list_for_each_entry_safe on &ops->list), so a NULL op->ops oopses. The\npath is reachable by any render-node fd holder, since NOUVEAU_VM_BIND is\nDRM_RENDER_ALLOW.\n\nGuard the free with IS_ERR_OR_NULL(), as nouveau_uvmm_bind_job_cleanup()\nalready does for the identical free.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8ec34618e71018fd7a3f73c57c6b92d71a6c7c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bf493cf7ed0c2b3df728977a257e0d99b4db1c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7dc03e09313d22a6d230b759de3b05d504c008f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3857238de6bce6c1573e8cb86c37b067e5208f05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/412a6ceb56d501ef2f8202e26ab4b5d4dfbca566"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89802", "GHSA-c2hc-j8hj-4mw2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "012a99a8-b650-39b9-b07a-2a214568422f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <b7dc03e09313d22a6d230b759de3b05d504c008f"}, {"id": "21ee3527-8efd-3bf3-b0c0-44d62f76e269", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "50db8ad7-7b09-3833-a685-bb6eb4364715", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5f2645ef-872e-378f-9cb1-c967a5952779", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "6e396d3e-de1e-3936-b6fd-e6b0b4a254b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cdbb63b6-9a20-341a-af44-9f3b2686c17b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <3857238de6bce6c1573e8cb86c37b067e5208f05"}, {"id": "d2f01be3-6961-3993-b7ae-d01a0f37550c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <3bf493cf7ed0c2b3df728977a257e0d99b4db1c6"}, {"id": "d703aa73-6c6a-35a8-a0f2-91fb55529bc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "e6734107-f3c7-32c7-9cc6-08fdc18045c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <412a6ceb56d501ef2f8202e26ab4b5d4dfbca566"}, {"id": "e8fc69fa-6be5-37d6-a5e7-1fd5cac29786", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "f39c7e3c-2536-321b-be6b-4abb0f7ec84a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <d8ec34618e71018fd7a3f73c57c6b92d71a6c7c3"}, {"id": "f6a305de-89e0-3b53-8162-56ceeace39d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bd409591-6571-362e-9094-159ffa01ee11", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}